{
  "id": "ee1-08",
  "number": 8,
  "title": "BJT: bias and the common-emitter amplifier",
  "topics": ["Discrete circuits", "Frequency response"],
  "goal": "Bias a 2N3904 with a voltage divider, check its DC operating point, then measure the small-signal gain of the common-emitter stage and the transistor's current gain β.",
  "theory": [
    "In the active region a BJT's collector current is β times its base current, and V_BE stays near 0.65–0.7 V. Output curves (I_C against V_CE, one per base current) are flat in the active region and collapse toward 0 V in saturation.",
    "Divider bias makes the base voltage nearly independent of β: V_B ≈ V_CC·R2/(R1 + R2) when the divider current is much larger than I_B. Then V_E = V_B − V_BE and I_C ≈ I_E = V_E/R_E (more exactly, add R_th/(β+1) of the divider to R_E) and V_C = V_CC − I_C·R_C.",
    "With an un-bypassed emitter resistor the mid-band voltage gain is A_v ≈ −R_C/(R_E + r_e), with r_e = 25 mV/I_C — close to −R_C/R_E. The minus sign is a 180° phase inversion.",
    "The input coupling capacitor blocks DC so the generator does not disturb the bias; it sets a low-frequency corner."
  ],
  "prelab": [
    { "key": "vb", "label": "Base voltage V_B (12 V, 47 kΩ / 10 kΩ)", "unit": "V", "answer": "12*10000/57000" },
    { "key": "ic", "label": "Collector current I_C (R_E = 1 kΩ)", "unit": "mA", "answer": "(12*10000/57000-0.7)/(1000+8246/161)*1000" },
    { "key": "vc", "label": "Collector voltage V_C (R_C = 4.7 kΩ)", "unit": "V", "answer": "12-4700*(12*10000/57000-0.7)/(1000+8246/161)" },
    { "key": "av", "label": "Mid-band gain magnitude |A_v|", "unit": "V/V", "answer": "4700/1000" }
  ],
  "procedure": [
    "Load the reference build. M1 reads the base (column 15) and M2 the collector (column 17), both against ground.",
    "Compare V_B, V_E (= V_B − V_BE) and V_C with your pre-lab — the transistor is in the active region when V_C is well above V_E.",
    "The generator injects 0.1 Vpp at 1 kHz through CIN. Scope CH1 on the input (column 10), CH2 on the collector with AC coupling. Gain = Vpp(CH2)/Vpp(CH1); note the inversion.",
    "Run Bench → Bode from h10 to e17 and find the low-frequency corner set by CIN.",
    "On the curve tracer (mode npn) trace Q2 and read β = I_C/I_B in the flat part of a curve."
  ],
  "table": [
    { "key": "vbm", "label": "Base voltage V_B", "unit": "V", "predict": "vb", "source": "dmm:M1" },
    { "key": "vcm", "label": "Collector voltage V_C", "unit": "V", "predict": "vc", "source": "dmm:M2", "tol": 8 },
    { "key": "avm", "label": "Gain |A_v| (CH2 Vpp / 0.1 V)", "unit": "V/V", "predict": "av", "source": "scope.ch2.vpp", "transform": "v/0.1", "tol": 12 }
  ],
  "checks": [
    { "kind": "dc", "label": "Divider sets the base voltage", "ref": "c15", "expect": "PS_v1*R2/(R1+R2)", "tol": 0.06 },
    { "kind": "dc", "label": "Emitter sits one V_BE below the base", "ref": "i19", "expect": "PS_v1*R2/(R1+R2)-0.7", "tol": 0.12 },
    { "kind": "dc", "label": "Collector voltage V_CC − I_C·R_C", "ref": "c17", "expect": "PS_v1-RC*(PS_v1*R2/(R1+R2)-0.7)/(RE+R1*R2/(R1+R2)/160)", "tol": 0.12 },
    { "kind": "bode", "label": "Mid-band gain ≈ R_C/R_E", "gen": "GEN", "in": "h10", "out": "c17", "metric": "gainAt", "f": 1000, "expect": "RC/RE", "tol": 0.15 },
    { "kind": "curve", "label": "β of the 2N3904 on the curve tracer", "tracer": "CT", "mode": "npn", "metric": "beta", "at": 0.00002, "expect": "160", "tol": 0.3 }
  ],
  "settle": 0.3,
  "callouts": [
    { "part": "Q1", "title": "2N3904 NPN", "text": "Gain ≈ R_C / R_E, inverted.", "icon": "chip" },
    { "part": "M1", "title": "BASE VOLTAGE", "text": "Set by the 47 k / 10 k divider.", "icon": "meter" },
    { "part": "CT", "title": "CURVE TRACER", "text": "Measures β on Q2.", "icon": "meter" }
  ],
  "build": {
